# Copy to .env and uncomment only the keys your run needs.
# `make fetch`, live-run Make targets and `bvb run` load the repository-root .env.
# `make verify-results`, `make validate`, `make smoke`, `make tool-smoke`, `make test`
# and `bvb score` need no keys. Public dataset downloads need no Hugging Face token.

# Gemini models (Gandalf and the host verifiers with gemini/ models; the paper's Flash runs).
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# OpenAI models (openai/ conditions). AAAJ also uses it for embeddings with any model.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Archipelago document extraction.
# REDUCTO_API_KEY=

# Daytona sandboxes for Gandalf and RewardKit conditions and snapshot builds.
# DAYTONA_API_KEY=

# Only for `make rewardkit-claude-smoke`.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Hugging Face: optional; a token only raises download rate limits.
# `make fetch` reads this value from .env. Alternatively, use `hf auth login` or
# export HF_TOKEN in your shell. Direct `python -m adapters.bvb.fetch` calls use
# the logged-in token or exported HF_TOKEN; they do not load .env.
# HF_TOKEN=
